    <front><contents /></front>
    <chapter>
      <heading>TTIOProgressSink functions</heading>
      <p></p>
      <function type="void(^" name="TTIOProgressBlock">
        <arg type="int64_t">done</arg>
        <arg type="int64_t">total</arg>
        <desc>
          <p>
            <em>Declared In:</em> Core/TTIOProgressSink.h
          </p>
          <p>
            Progress callback fired by long-running TTI-O
            readers and writers at meaningful chunk boundaries
            (per chromosome, per N reads, per spectrum) &#8212;
            not per byte &#8212; so the per-callback rate stays
            manageable.
          </p>
          <p>
            <code><var>done</var></code> is monotonically
            non-decreasing within a single operation.
            <code><var>total</var></code> is <code>-1</code>
            when the producer cannot predict the final count (e.g.
            streaming reads with no header); producers emit a
            final
            <code>(<var>total</var>, <var>total</var>)</code>
            fire once the true count is known.
          </p>
          <p>
            Implementations should be cheap and
            non-blocking; they may be invoked many times
            per second on a worker thread. GUI code needing to
            update the main thread must dispatch back upstream.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Cross-language equivalents:</strong>
            <br /> Java:
            <code>
              global.thalion.ttio.io.ProgressSink#onProgress(
              <strong>long</strong>,long)
            </code>
            <br /> Python:
            <code>ttio.io.progress.ProgressSinkLike</code>
          </p>
          @since 1.3.0
        </desc>
      </function>
    </chapter>
  </body>
</gsdoc>
